{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,500p' docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/00-foundation/007-verify.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"68a7de8d-5b7d-41e0-bddb-17183021e476\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec99b-0038-7f80-b3ec-637abc75b0ae\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019ec99b-0038-7f80-b3ec-637abc75b0ae\",\"storyId\":\"00-foundation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"00-foundation\",\"title\":\"Story 0: Foundation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/stories/00-foundation.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/tech-design.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/test-plan.md\",\"docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/06-derivation-recovery/artifacts/00-foundation/006-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/context.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/thread-migration.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification of Story 0 against AC-5.1 through AC-5.5, the derivation vocabulary rename DoD, v7 migration, public SDK logging surface, logging tests, and production fallback/logging paths.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S0-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Ready derivation rows still persist fallback markers instead of logging fallback events only\",\"evidence\":\"AC-5.3 requires a fallback event to exist only in the log and says ready derivation output must carry no degraded/fallback marker (00-foundation.md:43-48). Production turn derivation still collects fallback gaps and attaches them to ready turn_rendering writes (packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:83,95,106-115). Chunk summaries do the same (packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:164-175,192-200). The queue completion path persists those gaps on ready derivation rows (packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:304-312). `rg writeLog` found no production fallback call sites outside the SDK wrapper and logging tests, and TC-5.3a only manually inserts a clean derivation row before writing a log (packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts:93-143).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"TC-5.3a\",\"DD-5\",\"Story 0 DoD: no fallback marker on ready derivation outputs\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S0-F2\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"writeLog participates in the caller transaction\",\"evidence\":\"The story technical notes require `writeLog` to be fail-soft and not share the caller transaction (00-foundation.md:133-134), and DD-5 says it must not share the caller's transaction (tech-design.md:127-129). The implementation inserts through `ctx.db` directly (packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts:43-59). A focused rollback probe wrote a log inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, rolled back the caller transaction, and observed `{\\\"n\\\":0}` log rows; an independent log transaction would have left one row. TC-5.5a only injects a fake throwing prepare function, so it does not prove real-store transaction isolation (packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts:220-235).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.5\",\"TC-5.5a\",\"DD-5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S0-F3\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derivation vocabulary rename is not complete across current production/public shapes\",\"evidence\":\"Story 0 scope and DoD require the form vocabulary to be renamed across code and schema (00-foundation.md:15-18,162), and DD-1 says every reference changes from form to derivation vocabulary (tech-design.md:87-89). Current shared/public view and inspect shapes still expose `formUsed` and `formCounts` (packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:116-125,152; packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts:57,74). The compact production path persists those names into thread_view JSON (packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:458-479,508-514), and thread-view internals still define `FormSnapshot`/`FormLookup` for derivation state rows (packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts:131-145).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Story 0 Scope In: derivation vocabulary rename\",\"DD-1\",\"Story 0 DoD: rename complete across schema, types, work-queue kinds, and tests\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"S0-F1\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Ready derivation rows still persist fallback markers instead of logging fallback events only\",\"evidence\":\"AC-5.3 requires a fallback event to exist only in the log and says ready derivation output must carry no degraded/fallback marker (00-foundation.md:43-48). Production turn derivation still collects fallback gaps and attaches them to ready turn_rendering writes (packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:83,95,106-115). Chunk summaries do the same (packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:164-175,192-200). The queue completion path persists those gaps on ready derivation rows (packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:304-312). `rg writeLog` found no production fallback call sites outside the SDK wrapper and logging tests, and TC-5.3a only manually inserts a clean derivation row before writing a log (packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts:93-143).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"TC-5.3a\",\"DD-5\",\"Story 0 DoD: no fallback marker on ready derivation outputs\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S0-F2\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"writeLog participates in the caller transaction\",\"evidence\":\"The story technical notes require `writeLog` to be fail-soft and not share the caller transaction (00-foundation.md:133-134), and DD-5 says it must not share the caller's transaction (tech-design.md:127-129). The implementation inserts through `ctx.db` directly (packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts:43-59). A focused rollback probe wrote a log inside `BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, rolled back the caller transaction, and observed `{\\\"n\\\":0}` log rows; an independent log transaction would have left one row. TC-5.5a only injects a fake throwing prepare function, so it does not prove real-store transaction isolation (packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts:220-235).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/logging/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/logging-surface.test.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.5\",\"TC-5.5a\",\"DD-5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"S0-F3\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Derivation vocabulary rename is not complete across current production/public shapes\",\"evidence\":\"Story 0 scope and DoD require the form vocabulary to be renamed across code and schema (00-foundation.md:15-18,162), and DD-1 says every reference changes from form to derivation vocabulary (tech-design.md:87-89). Current shared/public view and inspect shapes still expose `formUsed` and `formCounts` (packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts:116-125,152; packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts:57,74). The compact production path persists those names into thread_view JSON (packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts:458-479,508-514), and thread-view internals still define `FormSnapshot`/`FormLookup` for derivation state rows (packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts:131-145).\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/inspect.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"Story 0 Scope In: derivation vocabulary rename\",\"DD-1\",\"Story 0 DoD: rename complete across schema, types, work-queue kinds, and tests\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"fresh-fix-path\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-5.1 / TC-5.1a: info, warning, and error log levels are persisted by the SDK logging path and covered by logging-surface.test.ts.\",\"AC-5.2 / TC-5.2a: internal writeLog and SDK instance logging.write write to the same durable log table in logging-surface.test.ts.\",\"AC-5.3 / TC-5.3b: failed derivation state and reason remain on the derivation row independent of log entries in logging-surface.test.ts.\",\"AC-5.4 / TC-5.4a: queryLog supports